            "authorName": "surendra",
            "body": "\n![Screenshot 2026-07-30 at 8.16.04 PM.png](data:image/jpeg;base64,)\n#### Problem\nRight now, there's no working way to filter issues by author, label, milestone, assignee, or open/closed status on the mobile app's repository detail screen. The **Issues** tab currently renders the entire list of published issues without any interactive filtering controls or state.\n\n#### Root Cause\nIn `RepoDetailScreen.dart`, `_IssuesTab` is implemented as a simple `StatelessWidget` using `_AsyncList<Issue>`:\n* It dumps the raw payload from `api.publishedIssues(...)` straight into the list.\n* There is no local state (`StatefulWidget`) to track selected filter criteria.\n* There is no UI component (like a filter bar or dropdowns) to select authors, labels, milestones, or assignees.\n* No client-side filtering logic is being applied before rendering the issue cards.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\nUsers should be able to filter the repository's issue list smoothly from a horizontal filter bar at the top of the tab:\n1. **Status:** Filter by *Open*, *Closed*, or *All*.\n2. **Dynamic Dropdowns:** Filter by *Label*, *Author*, *Milestone*, or *Assignee*, populated automatically from the unique metadata present in the fetched issues.\n3. **Reset:** A quick \"Reset\" / \"Clear\" button to wipe active filters.\n4. **State Persistence:** Filter selections should survive tab switching (e.g., jumping between Code, Issues, and Pulls) without resetting.\n\n#### Proposed Solution\n* **Convert `_IssuesTab` to a `StatefulWidget`** and mix in `AutomaticKeepAliveClientMixin` (`wantKeepAlive => true`) so filter state doesn't get destroyed when changing tabs.\n* **Add a horizontal filter bar** at the top of the `ListView` with dropdowns for Status, Label, Author, Milestone, and Assignee.\n* **Cache sorted metadata options** (`_authors`, `_labels`, etc.) when the API payload loads so we don't re-sort arrays on every filter click.\n* **Apply an `O(n)` client-side filter** against `allIssues` inside `_filterIssues(...)` before rendering the `_MobileCard` list.",
